---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Use | Free AI Background Remover';
const description =
  'Plain-language terms for the free in-browser background remover: local processing, no warranty, and your responsibility for the images you use.';
const email = (import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL ?? '').trim();
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p>Last updated October 26, 2026.</p>
    <p>
      This free tool removes backgrounds in your web browser. By using the site you agree to these
      terms. If you do not agree, don’t use the site. These terms are a plain-language agreement
      from the site operator. They are not a substitute for advice from your own lawyer.
    </p>

    <h2>The service</h2>
    <p>
      The page lets you pick an image, run the public ISNet int8 model on your device, and download
      a transparent PNG. There is no account and no fee charged by this site. Processing happens
      locally. Output quality varies. Hair, glass, fine detail, and unusual subjects can look wrong.
      You are responsible for checking the PNG before you publish it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your images</h2>
    <p>
      You keep whatever rights you already have in images you process. You confirm that you have
      the rights needed to use those images this way. Don’t use the tool to infringe copyright,
      violate privacy, or break the law. The site operator does not receive a copy of your image
      through the tool and does not review cutouts.
    </p>

    <h2>The model and the software</h2>
    <p>
      The segmentation weights come from the Apache-2.0 project
      <a href="https://huggingface.co/chenjindu/isnet-web">chenjindu/isnet-web</a>. The browser
      preprocess and composite follow the Apache-2.0 reference implementation linked from that model
      card. Those upstream licenses still apply to those parts. The website does not grant you a
      license to anyone else’s photos, trademarks, or publicity rights.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Don’t attack the site, the model host, or other people through this service.</li>
      <li>Don’t bypass technical limits in order to disrupt the static hosting.</li>
      <li>Don’t present the cutout as a guaranteed, official, or human-reviewed edit.</li>
      <li>Don’t use the tool where a mistake in the matte could cause harm you are not willing to own.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site is provided as-is and as-available. It may be slow, wrong, interrupted, or withdrawn.
      To the extent the law allows, the operator disclaims warranties of merchantability, fitness
      for a particular purpose, and non-infringement. The operator is not liable for lost profits,
      lost files, or decisions you make from a cutout. Some places do not allow these limits. In
      those places, the limits apply only as far as the law permits. The operator’s total liability
      for a claim about the site is limited to zero, because the tool is offered at no charge,
      unless a law requires otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2>Disputes and changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms do not pick a court or a governing-law clause, because the operator has not
      published one. If you have a problem, contact us first and describe what happened.
      {email ? (
        <> Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.</>
      ) : (
        <> Publish <code>PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL</code> so people can reach the operator.</>
      )}
      The operator may update the site and these terms by changing the published pages. The date
      above tracks the current text.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
